  "gettingStarted": {
    "title": "Getting started",
    "body": "Pick a duration (F1-F6), then click a fret on the guitar keyboard or type its number to place a note. Use the chord wheel to drop in full chords. Undo/redo, cut/copy/paste, and the effect shortcuts all work while you play — check Help > Keyboard shortcuts for the full list."
  },
  "notationGuide": {
    "title": "Tab notation guide",
    "body": "Bends draw an upward arrow with the target interval; slides draw a diagonal line between frets; vibrato is a wavy line above the note; h/p marks a hammer-on or pull-off between two notes on the same string; x marks a dead/muted note; a note in parentheses is a ghost note; brackets under a passage mark palm muting; a dashed tie marks let-ring."
  },
